=== 1. Static pull from the lattice constraints (GR point J=2ks, g=1/(2ks), ks=16 pi G, G=1) ===
axis r= 2.00: n=-0.50942 (-GM/r=-0.50000) r= 4.00: n=-0.22544 (-GM/r=-0.25000) r= 8.00: n=-0.09611 (-GM/r=-0.12500) r=12.00: n=-0.05428 (-GM/r=-0.08333) r=16.00: n=-0.03364 (-GM/r=-0.06250)
diag r= 1.73: n=-0.51807 (-GM/r=-0.57735) r= 3.46: n=-0.25512 (-GM/r=-0.28868) r= 6.93: n=-0.11439 (-GM/r=-0.14434) r=10.39: n=-0.06677 (-GM/r=-0.09623) r=13.86: n=-0.04300 (-GM/r=-0.07217)
psi + n = 0 identically: 0.0
(differences from -GM/r at small r are the lattice Green function's cubic O(a^2/r^2) terms plus the
 finite-torus neutralising background ~ r^2/L^3; the 1/r tail is the standard lattice Coulomb law.)

