=== 5. Universality: active and passive couplings both through T00 = energy density ===
m=0.2: passive coefficient of n per unit rest energy = 1.00000000, of psi = -6.99e-07; active: sources S/ks = -T00, one quantum at rest has sum T00 = omega = 0.2000, sum T_ij = 0
m=0.8: passive coefficient of n per unit rest energy = 1.00000000, of psi = -4.65e-07; active: sources S/ks = -T00, one quantum at rest has sum T00 = omega = 0.8000, sum T_ij = 0
m=1.5: passive coefficient of n per unit rest energy = 1.00000000, of psi = -4.56e-07; active: sources S/ks = -T00, one quantum at rest has sum T00 = omega = 1.5000, sum T_ij = 0

=== 6. TT self-energy at q -> 0 from the LINEAR coupling only (paramagnetic, vacuum, per site) ===
Nb=48 m=0.0: d2E0/deps2 per site: E-channel -0.003694, T2-channel -0.011782  (ratio 0.3136; isotropic would need XE^2 avg = XT^2 avg/... )
Nb=48 m=0.5: d2E0/deps2 per site: E-channel -0.003172, T2-channel -0.010574  (ratio 0.3000; isotropic would need XE^2 avg = XT^2 avg/... )
Nb=48 m=1.0: d2E0/deps2 per site: E-channel -0.002317, T2-channel -0.008228  (ratio 0.2816; isotropic would need XE^2 avg = XT^2 avg/... )
Nb=96 m=0.0: d2E0/deps2 per site: E-channel -0.003695, T2-channel -0.011782  (ratio 0.3136; isotropic would need XE^2 avg = XT^2 avg/... )
Nb=96 m=0.5: d2E0/deps2 per site: E-channel -0.003172, T2-channel -0.010574  (ratio 0.3000; isotropic would need XE^2 avg = XT^2 avg/... )
Nb=96 m=1.0: d2E0/deps2 per site: E-channel -0.002317, T2-channel -0.008228  (ratio 0.2816; isotropic would need XE^2 avg = XT^2 avg/... )
Both channels are nonzero and unequal: the linear-order first-class coupling leaves a cubic-anisotropic
TT 'mass' at O(kappa) unless an O(h^2) seagull is added.  Ward identity for constant strain: with
U = exp(-i sum xi.P), xi_i = h_ij x_j/2, U H_m U^+ = H_m - 1/2 h.sum T + O(h^2) [identity (M)], so E0 is h-independent
iff the O(h^2) term equals 1/2[S,[S,H_m]]; then Pi_TT(0) = para + seagull = 0 by the f-sum identity.
